course: dictionary
lesson: 9057
title: One word, two meanings: sleeve
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning a number, and the sentence tells you which one is being used. «Roll up sleeves and tie back long hair before cooking.» Here a sleeve is the part of a shirt or jumper that covers your arm, because you roll it up.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Bottle labels are printed on long rolls and glued on, or a plastic tube called a shrink sleeve is pulled over the bottle and shrunk tight in a hot tunnel.» The word «shrink sleeve» tells you a sleeve can also be a cover that fits over something, not only over an arm.
explain: Phrases use a word in a special way. «To have something up your sleeve» means to have a secret plan or trick ready. You cannot find this meaning by looking at the word alone, so the phrase must be learnt as a whole.
fact: A sleeve is the part of a shirt, coat or jumper that covers your arm.
fact: A sleeve is also a cover or case for something flat, like a record, a laptop or a card.
fact: «Long sleeves» and «short sleeves» describe how far the sleeve reaches down your arm.
fact: «Roll up your sleeves» means get ready to work hard.
fact: «Up your sleeve» means a secret plan or trick you are keeping hidden.
exercise: «Roll up long sleeves and tie back long hair before cooking.» What is a sleeve in this sentence? | A pan used for frying | A tube of hot plastic | A kind of hat worn in the kitchen | *The part of a shirt, coat or jumper that covers your arm
exercise: A story says, «She had a plan up her sleeve.» What does up your sleeve mean? | A piece of clothing that is too short | *A secret plan or trick | Something wet and cold | A loud song
exercise: Which meaning of sleeve is used in «a plastic tube called a shrink sleeve is pulled over the bottle»? | A sort of collar | *A cover or case that fits over something | The part of a shirt that covers your arm | A kind of bottle
test: «Long sleeves» and «short sleeves» tell you how far a sleeve reaches down your arm. What does «roll up your sleeves» mean? | Hide something in your coat | *Get ready to work hard | Take off your clothes to swim | Wash your hands very slowly
test: Ella reads, «The record was kept safe in its sleeve.» Which meaning of sleeve fits? | A secret plan | A kind of bottle label | *A cover or case for something flat, like a record | The part of a shirt that covers your arm
exam: Ben says, «I have a trick up my sleeve.» Explain in your own words what he means, and say which meaning of sleeve is NOT used here. | A trick with a magic card, and the record cover is used here | He is rolling up his shirt, and the secret plan is not used here | He has a long coat, and the phrase means very cold | *A secret plan, and the arm part of a shirt is not used here
